  <data name="DisksLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Disks</value>
  </data>
  <data name="EssentialServicesLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Essential services</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SecurityScoreTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Güvenlik Puanı</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RefreshButton.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Yenile</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UninstallButton.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Uninstall</value>
  </data>
  <data name="AdminRequiredInfoBar.Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Administrator required</value>
  </data>
  <data name="AdminRequiredInfoBar.Message" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Changing this startup item requires an administrator. Restart BECETTI SECURITY as administrator from Ayarlar.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TitleStartup.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Startup Manager</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SubtitleStartup.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Real registry startup entries — the same Run-key and Task Manager convention Windows itself uses. No performance impact score is invented: Windows does not expose one through any stable API.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TitleSoftware.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Software Manager</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SubtitleSoftware.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Real installed applications from the Windows registry — the same list Ayarlar &gt; Apps shows. Uninstalling only launches the application's own real uninstaller; nothing is removed directly.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TitleDrivers.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Driver Monitor</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SubtitleDrivers.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Real installed device drivers from Windows (WMI), the same inventory Cihaz Manager uses. BECETTI SECURITY has no driver issue database of its own — check Windows Güncelle or the manufacturer's site for updates.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TitleUsb.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>USB Protection</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SubtitleUsb.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Real connected removable drives and Windows' own AutoPlay/AutoRun policy, which blocks the classic autorun.inf USB-malware vector. Scanning a drive runs through Microsoft Defender — BECETTI SECURITY has no USB scanning engine of its own.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UsbConnectedDrivesLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Connected Removable Drives</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ScanSelectedDriveButton.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Scan Selected Drive with Defender</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UsbAutoRunLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>AutoPlay / AutoRun Protection</value>
  </data>
  <data name="EnableAutoRunProtectionButton.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enable AutoRun Protection</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DisableAutoRunProtectionButton.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Remove BECETTI's AutoRun Block</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TitleNetwork.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ağ Monitor</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SubtitleNetwork.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Real network adapters and active TCP connections, read from Windows' own NetworkInterface API and Get-NetTCPConnection (the same source Resource Monitor uses). BECETTI SECURITY draws no conclusion about any connection — it shows Windows' own verified list.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="FirewallProfilesLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Güvenlik Duvarı Profiles</value>
  </data>
  <data name="NetworkAdaptersLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ağ Adapters</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ActiveConnectionsLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Aktif Connections &amp; Listening Ports</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TitleEmergency.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Emergency Center</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SubtitleEmergency.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A single place for 'something feels wrong' moments — real status, quick access to Windows' own tools, and BECETTI AI for help.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="QuickActionsLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Quick actions</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OpenThreatsButton.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>View Threats</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OpenWindowsSecurityButton.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Open Windows Güvenlik</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OpenBackupSettingsButton.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Backup &amp; Recovery</value>
  </data>
  <data name="AskBecettiAiButton.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ask BECETTI AI</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DiagnosticSummaryLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Diagnostic summary</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DiagnosticSummaryHint.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Builds a plain-text snapshot of your current protection, firewall and PC health state for you to copy — nothing is sent anywhere automatically.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="GenerateSummaryButton.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Generate Summary</value>
  </data>
  <data name="NavVulnerability.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Zafiyet Danışmanı</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TitleVulnerability.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Vulnerability Advisor</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SubtitleVulnerability.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A combined view of real checks already performed elsewhere in BECETTI SECURITY (Defender, firewall, USB AutoRun, drivers, TPM, Secure Boot, BitLocker, Windows Güncelle). There is no separate vulnerability scanner or CVE database — every finding traces back to a named real check.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="VulnerabilityFindingsLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Findings</value>
  </data>
  <data name="NavBrowser.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Tarayıcı Güvenliği</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TitleBrowser.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Browser Güvenlik</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SubtitleBrowser.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Real installed browsers (from the same installed-apps inventory Software Manager reads) and Windows' own SmartScreen policy, read from the registry.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SmartScreenLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>SmartScreen</value>
  </data>
  <data name="InstalledBrowsersLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Installed Browsers</value>
  </data>
  <data name="NavIdentity.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Kimlik Koruması</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TitleIdentity.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Identity Protection</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SubtitleIdentity.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Real hardware/platform security that protects your credentials and data at rest: TPM, Secure Boot, Credential Guard and BitLocker, read from Get-Tpm, Confirm-SecureBootUEFI, Win32_DeviceGuard and Get-BitLockerVolume.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="NavWifi.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Wi-Fi Güvenliği</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TitleWifi.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Wi-Fi Güvenlik</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SubtitleWifi.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The real authentication and cipher of the Wi-Fi network you're currently connected to, read from netsh wlan show interfaces — the same tool Windows' own Wi-Fi diagnostics use.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="NavScheduledScan.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Zamanlanmış Taramalar</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TitleScheduledScan.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Scheduled Scan</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SubtitleScheduledScan.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Registers a real Windows Scheduled Task (visible and editable in Task Scheduler) that runs a genuine Microsoft Defender scan daily — even while BECETTI SECURITY is closed. Creating or removing it requires an administrator.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ScheduleNewScanLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Schedule a daily scan</value>
  </data>
  <data name="FullScanToggle.Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Full scan (otherwise Quick scan)</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ScheduleHourLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Hour of day (0-23, local time)</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ScheduleScanButton.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Schedule</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RemoveScheduleButton.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Remove Scheduled Scan</value>
  </data>
  <data name="NavBackup.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Yedekleme Danışmanı</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TitleBackup.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Backup Advisor</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SubtitleBackup.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Windows' own real backup posture: File History's service state and Sistem Geri Yükle's real shadow copies. BECETTI SECURITY implements no backup engine of its own — antivirus protection is not a substitute for backups.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="NavReports.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Güvenlik Raporları</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TitleReports.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Smart Güvenlik Reports</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SubtitleReports.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A consolidated snapshot assembled from checks that already exist elsewhere in BECETTI SECURITY (Defender, firewall, Vulnerability Advisor). Dışa Aktar it as plain text or a simple PDF to share or archive.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SaveAsPdfButton.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Kaydet as PDF</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SaveAsTextButton.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Kaydet as Text</value>
  </data>
  <data name="NavCloudSync.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bulut Eşitleme</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TitleCloudSync.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Cloud Sync</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SubtitleCloudSync.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Real connectivity and sign-in status for your BECETTI cloud account. This is a status view on top of the existing cloud sign-in — there is no second backend or data store being synchronized.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SyncNowButton.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Sync Now</value>
  </data>
  <data name="NavKnowledge.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bilgi Bankası</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TitleKnowledge.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Knowledge Base</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SubtitleKnowledge.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Locally-authored articles explaining the real security features BECETTI SECURITY exposes and general safe-use practices. No network call is made to show this content.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="KnowledgeSearchBox.PlaceholderText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ara articles...</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SearchButton.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ara</value>
  </data>
  <data name="NavThreatIntel.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Tehdit İstihbaratı</value>
  </data>
  <data name="TitleThreatIntel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Tehdit Intelligence</value>
  </data>
  <data name="SubtitleThreatIntel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>An optional second opinion from VirusTotal's ~70 third-party antivirus engines for a file or link you choose — including a suspicious email attachment you saved, or a link from an email or message before you open it. This never replaces Microsoft Defender, BECETTI SECURITY's own independent protection engine — it is a separate, clearly-labelled check you run on demand.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ThreatIntelNotConfiguredBar.Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Not configured</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ThreatIntelNotConfiguredBar.Message" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The threat-intelligence server is not configured. Open Ayarlar and set the BECETTI server URL.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ThreatIntelFileSectionLabel.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Scan a file</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ThreatIntelScanFileButton.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Check hash</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ThreatIntelHashOnlyNote.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The file's SHA-256 is computed on this device and checked against VirusTotal's database — the file itself is not uploaded for this step.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ThreatIntelUploadConsentBar.Title" xml:space="preserve">
